			"type": "text",
			"text": "Coming from the Late Permian of South Africa, Austroprosboloides vandijki was a rather large and primitive species of cicada, closely related to the larger and more well-known palaeontinids of the Mesozoic period. It was discovered in deposits of the Estcourt Formation, corresponding to the Daptocephalus Assemblage Zone."
		},
		{
			"advancement": "lepidodendron:pf_adv_book_palaeontinid_austroprosboloides",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Contrarily to the more derived Late Mesozoic palaeontinids, Austroprosboloides and its relatives had more limited flight capabilities, with smaller forewings and larger hindwings."
